<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stok Palace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stok Palace is a royal palace in the village of Stok, south of Leh in Ladakh, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the far side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>. Built in the early 19th century, it became the residence of the Namgyal royal family after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dogras">Dogra</a> conquest of Ladakh and remains their home. Part of it is a museum of royal regalia, costumes and thangkas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stok-palace.jpg" alt="Stok Palace" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Baldiri · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stok_palau_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
